  "description": "Gives a holding of an ETF that is no security of the database its Yahoo symbol, the key of the sector map. A provider listing (ticker + exchange, as the provider names the exchange; compared after lower-casing and dropping everything but letters and digits) becomes: ticker in upper case, a space or dot inside becomes '-', a numeric ticker zero-padded to 'pad' digits, plus 'suffix'. An exchange is listed only where the provider's exchange name stands for exactly one Yahoo market; the rest is under not_mapped with the reason and gives no symbol. A holding that the provider publishes with an ISIN only takes the reviewed symbol of that ISIN from the private etf_listing_symbols_local.json (isin_symbols: {ISIN: symbol}). Used only by the sector overview, after the security and the ISIN of the company found no sector; the matching of the effective exposure does not read this file. The sector itself always comes from the sector map.",
